  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-werewolf",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nAn AI-powered Werewolf game for the DeepSeek Harness Web UI. Watch a complete AI game or join one seat as a human player."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- 6, 9, and 12-seat games.\n- AI-only spectator mode and single-human participation mode.\n- Werewolf, Seer, Witch, Villager, Guard, and Hunter roles.\n- Sheriff election, badge transfer, speeches, voting, tie-break rounds, and night actions.\n- Uses the model currently selected in DeepSeek Harness."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "After the first npm release, install the prebuilt package into the Web profile, then restart DSH Web:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-werewolf --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/\ndsh web\n```\n\nFor local development:\n\n```sh\npnpm install --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/\npnpm run check\ndsh plugin --profile web add .\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm run typecheck\npnpm run test\npnpm run build\nnpm pack --dry-run\n\nThe Host entry is maintained in `src/index.js` and copied to `lib/index.js` during the build. TypeScript domain modules compile into `lib/`, and `src/client/index.js` is bundled into the browser entry at `client/client.js`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Runtime scope",
      "text": "The game is process-local and currently supports one active game per DSH Web process. Its RPC channel is loopback-only. Restarting the DSH process discards the active game."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
